---
import Layout from '../../studio/layouts/Layout.astro';
import { mailto, studio } from '../../apps/registry';

const title = 'Support — Paperdot';
const description = 'Support and contact for Paperdot by Yaner Apps.';

// One tap opens a mail draft with the report fields already laid out.
const template =
  `mailto:${studio.email}?` +
  new URLSearchParams({
    subject: 'Paperdot: ',
    body: [
      'Device model: ',
      'Android version: ',
      'Paperdot version (Android Settings → Apps → Paperdot): ',
      '',
      'What I did:',
      '',
      'What I expected:',
      '',
      'What happened instead:',
      '',
    ].join('\n'),
  })
    .toString()
    .replace(/\+/g, '%20');
---

<Layout title={title} description={description}>
  <div class="prose">
    <nav aria-label="Paperdot navigation" class="product-nav">
      <a href="/support">Support by app</a> <span aria-hidden="true">/</span> Paperdot
      <span> · </span><a href="/paperdot/privacy">Privacy</a>
    </nav>
    <div class="prose-header">
      <h1>Support</h1>
      <p class="lede">Questions, bug reports, and privacy requests for Paperdot.</p>
      <div class="meta">
        <span>Updated: 30 Oct 2026</span>
      </div>
    </div>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>
      Email <a href={mailto()}>{studio.email}</a>. To help us reproduce a
      problem, please include:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>Your device model and Android version</li>
      <li>The app version (Android Settings &rarr; Apps &rarr; Paperdot)</li>
      <li>What you did, what you expected, and what happened instead</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Please don't send your journal or a backup file unless we ask for it; a description of the problem is
      usually enough.
    </p>
    <p><a class="button" href={template}>Start an email with these fields</a></p>

    <h2>Common questions</h2>

    <h3>How do I move my journal to a new phone?</h3>
    <p>
      Make a backup in <strong>Profile &rarr; Back up &amp; restore</strong>, copy the <code>.paperdot.json</code> file to the
      new phone, and restore it there from the same screen. Restoring first backs up whatever journal is already
      on that phone, so nothing is lost by accident.
    </p>

    <h3>My reminders arrive late or not at all</h3>
    <p>
      Allow notifications for Paperdot, then go to <strong>Settings &rarr; Apps &rarr; Paperdot &rarr; Battery</strong>
      (or <strong>App battery usage</strong>) and select <strong>Unrestricted</strong>. Some devices hold back
      reminders from apps they put to sleep.
    </p>

    <h3>My calendar events don't show up</h3>
    <p>
      Paperdot shows events only from the calendars you pick in its settings, and only after you allow calendar
      access. Events from an account appear once Android has synced that account's calendar.
    </p>

    <h3>Why can't I migrate all my tasks at once?</h3>
    <p>
      That's on purpose. In the Bullet Journal method, rewriting each task by hand is when you decide whether it
      still matters. The review walks you through tasks one at a time, and <strong>Later</strong> always takes
      you straight back to your journal.
    </p>

    <h3>I subscribed to Pro but still see the free limits</h3>
    <p>
      Open <strong>Profile &rarr; Paperdot Pro &rarr; Restore purchase</strong> while online, signed in to the
      Google account you subscribed with. On a new device or after reinstalling, Paperdot checks with Google
      Play the first time it can.
    </p>

    <h3>What happens to my journal if Pro ends?</h3>
    <p>
      Nothing is deleted or changed. Trackers you made stay readable and editable, and your paper and font
      choices come back if you subscribe again.
    </p>

    <h3>How do I delete my data?</h3>
    <p>
      Your journal is stored only on your device. Delete entries in the app, or uninstall Paperdot to remove
      everything. Backup files you saved elsewhere are yours to delete.
    </p>
  </div>
</Layout>
